    {
      "id": "openai-token-expiry-monitor-0001",
      "name": "OpenAI Token Expiry Monitor",
      "agentId": "ops",
      "enabled": false,
      "schedule": {
        "kind": "cron",
        "cron": "0 9 * * *"
      },
      "payload": {
        "prompt": "Check OpenAI Codex token expiry. Run this Python snippet and report:\n\nimport json, datetime, base64\ntry:\n    with open('../agents/main/agent/auth-profiles.json') as f:\n        profiles = json.load(f)\n    expiring = []\n    for name, p in profiles['profiles'].items():\n        if p.get('provider') == 'openai-codex' and p.get('expires'):\n            exp_ms = p['expires']\n            exp_dt = datetime.datetime.fromtimestamp(exp_ms/1000)\n            days_left = (exp_dt - datetime.datetime.now()).days\n            expiring.append((name, exp_dt.strftime('%Y-%m-%d'), days_left))\n    for name, exp, days in sorted(expiring, key=lambda x: x[2]):\n        status = 'EXPIRED' if days < 0 else ('URGENT' if days < 3 else ('WARNING' if days < 7 else 'OK'))\n        print(f'{status}: {name} expires {exp} ({days}d)')\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f'Error: {e}')\n\nIf any account shows EXPIRED or URGENT, post a Slack message to #redos-ops saying: 'ACTION NEEDED: OpenAI Codex account [name] has expired or expires in <3 days. Run: openclaw models auth login to re-authenticate.' Otherwise just log 'All OpenAI tokens OK' to workspace/logs/token-health.log with a timestamp."
      },
      "state": {
        "scheduleErrorCount": 5,
        "consecutiveErrors": 0,
        "lastStatus": "pending",
        "lastRunStatus": "pending"
      }
    },
